# Your definition of “done” on May 8

Do not judge success by whether every imaginable feature exists. Judge it by whether a real visitor can use both websites safely and clearly.

## Nonprofit site is done when

- A visitor understands HopeStand’s mission within 30 seconds.
- They can learn about programs and work.
- They can contact HopeStand.
- They can donate or follow the donation process.
- They can find the marketplace.
- The site works on phones and desktop.
- You can update content without breaking the layout.

## Marketplace is done when

- A customer can find a product.
- They can see accurate product information and price.
- They can add a product to cart.
- They can complete checkout.
- They receive an order confirmation.
- You receive an order notification.
- You can manage orders and inventory.
- Customers can find shipping, return, refund, privacy, and support information.
- The site works on mobile.
- You have tested backup restoration and updates.

